sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two numbers are relatively prime, then the product of one of them with itself is relatively prime to the remaining one.
----
proof:

Let {A} and {B} be two numbers relatively prime, and let {A} multiplied by itself make {C}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="130" height="250" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VII.25 diagram" src="propVII25.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // A and B relatively prime, C the product of A with itself, D made equal
    // to A. Line segments only, so the walk is highlight beats; D is drawn
    // when the proof makes it.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): the lineSlider ends A1, A2,
    // B1, B2, C1, D1 and the off-canvas, colourless rail ends and unit U1,
